<!--
 Copyright (c) 2026 Hachist Robotics
 Author: wanglei@hachist.com
 上海哈船智能船舶技术有限公司
 File: package.xml
 Brief: Manifest for quadruped -- plain-CMake package (build_type cmake)

 Description:
 quadruped is the single process that touches the M20S chassis (13 S1.1). It
 will link rclcpp for one edge only -- the ROS 2 uplink of channel three -- and
 that edge does not exist yet, so the package declares build_type cmake and no
 ROS dependency today. When batch B8 adds the uplink the dependency is added
 here as an <exec_depend>, and the CMakeLists already guards it with
 find_package so a host without ROS keeps building the core and its tests.

 Why not ament_cmake now, given the package will end up using rclcpp: an ament
 package cannot be configured at all without a ROS environment, which would
 make the ROS-free core untestable on any machine that lacks one. The core is
 where every unit test lives, so it must stay independently buildable.
-->
<package format="3">
  <name>quadruped</name>
  <version>0.1.0</version>
  <description>M20S chassis interface and Tier 1 safety backstop (13)</description>
  <maintainer email="wanglei@hachist.com">wanglei</maintainer>
  <license>Apache-2.0</license>

  <buildtool_depend>cmake</buildtool_depend>

  <export>
    <build_type>cmake</build_type>
  </export>
</package>
